ollamarun - a full `ollama run` wrapper with rendering and saved sessions

Version: 2.9

Summary of changes in this version:
  - Interactive inline sessions now run in a detached per-session host. The
    host owns the Repl (session, slash commands, turns, tool loop, approvals,
    pulls, summarization and auto-compaction); the terminal is a thin client
    over a Unix socket. Closing the window or pressing Ctrl+C twice within
    10s while work runs detaches without cancelling anything, and
    `ollamarun -c` reattaches: a running turn is replayed from the start and
    continues live, a turn that finished while away is shown under "while
    you were away", and pending approvals/questions are asked again. A
    second terminal takes over cleanly. `/bye`, Ctrl+D, `--close-session` and
    `--delete` are the explicit closes; `--no-background` (or config
    `background_sessions: false`) restores the foreground REPL. One-shots
    and the TUI are unchanged. Under the hood: `session_host.py`/`host_client.py`,
    routed rich output, a `Renderer.begin/feed/end` event path and the
    `background_*` config keys.

Version: 2.8

Summary of changes in this version:
  - A response format now steps the whole harness aside, not just the tool
    schemas: with `--format` set (or on a resumed session that carries one)
    the system prompt leaves the tool rules out, the runtime skips its
    tool-support check and extra rounds, `session_info` reports tools off,
    and `/tools` shows every tool off with the reason instead of listing
    them as on. One `Repl.tools_active()` predicate decides for all of them;
    the `--json --format` path no longer needs its own override.

Version: 2.7

Summary of changes in this version:
  - A bad `--image` path says what is wrong: `image not found: PATH`, or
    `cannot attach image PATH: …` for an empty or unreadable file, instead
    of printing only the bare path. The image loop moved into a testable
    `attach_images()` and the images page documents the message.

Version: 2.6

Summary of changes in this version:
  - An `@file` mention no longer swallows trailing sentence punctuation:
    `@/tmp/notes.txt.` inlines `notes.txt` and leaves the `.` in the
    prompt, with the path as typed still tried first so a file whose name
    really ends in punctuation keeps resolving. The mentions page now
    describes the rule instead of the old failure.

Version: 2.5

Summary of changes in this version:
  - `--export-format html` (and `/export --format html`) writes only the HTML
    document: the recording console gets an in-memory sink, so the rendered
    transcript no longer leaks to the terminal before (or alongside) the
    export.

Version: 2.4

Summary of changes in this version:
  - Machine-readable stdout is byte-verbatim. `--json`, `--csv` and
    `--markdown` (the list/search/show/export flags and the chat/embedding
    `--json` modes) write straight to stdout instead of through the rich
    console, so a long title, answer or field is never soft-wrapped with a
    real newline that corrupts the payload.

Version: 2.3

Summary of changes in this version:
  - `-c` no longer swallows a prompt that matches a stored session title.
    A token is read as a session reference only for an exact id, an id
    prefix, or an exact title with a separate prompt following it; a lone
    token that contains or equals a title stays the prompt, so reusing
    prompt wording continues the latest session as documented.

Version: 2.2

Summary of changes in this version:
  - A flag between MODEL and PROMPT is no longer unrecognized: the CLI parses
    with `parse_intermixed_args`, so `ollamarun qwen3:0.6b --no-tools "hi"`
    (and every other flag-first/middle/last order the help shows) runs the
    one-shot. Positionals and option values parse exactly as before in every
    form that already worked.

Version: 2.1

Summary of changes in this version:
  - Mid-stream backend errors are reported instead of crashing the app. Both
    error paths passed the unsupported rich `stderr=` keyword to
    `Console.print`, so a stream that started and then failed raised a
    `TypeError` that hid the backend message (and a failed unload warning
    did the same). The error line now goes through a real stderr console in
    `--raw` mode and a failed unload warning follows its `quiet` flag; a
    one-shot mid-stream error prints the message and exits 1, and the REPL
    stays alive.

Version: 2.0

Summary of changes in this version:
  - The API layer is complete, and this release marks it as the supported
    contract: ollamarun is now both the terminal harness it always was and a
    reusable agent backend. One runtime drives all three front ends — the
    REPL, the TUI and `ollamarun serve` — and the version jumps to 2.0
    because that surface (and the behavior pinned with it) is a stable,
    tested interface rather than an experiment.
  - `ollamarun serve` is the whole surface. OpenAI-compatible: `GET
    /v1/models`, `GET /v1/models/{id}`, `POST /v1/embeddings` (float and
    base64 encodings) and `POST /v1/chat/completions` (streaming SSE,
    `n > 1`, `parallel_tool_calls`, client `tools` passed through and never
    executed), with strict validation, structured errors, thinking as
    `delta.reasoning_content`, and the permanently unsupported features
    recorded rather than guessed at. Native agent API: typed turn events
    with replay and `stream.gap`, explicit approval state, session CRUD,
    artifact upload/download with provenance, and context/placement control
    (`num_ctx`/`gpu_layers`, synchronous fit estimates, asynchronous probe
    jobs).
  - The operational contract ships with it: the validated `serve_*`
    configuration matrix, LAN/tailnet-only binding without authentication
    (deferred by design, never a substitute for tool approval), the
    workspace jail and artifact-root containment, aggregate input limits,
    chunked request decoding, the `serve_models` allowlist and the
    `serve_agent` switch, and an ordered shutdown that drains handlers and
    unloads only the models the server used.
  - Everything is gated: the two-file suite (`python3 test_ollamarun.py`)
    with the required pyflakes and official-SDK gates, the in-process fake
