    an optional `--live` real-backend pass, and the runnable reference
    clients in `examples/`.

Version: 1.59

Summary of changes in this version:
  - Phase 8: the API layer is documented and demonstrated end to end. Two
    reference clients land under `examples/`: `openai_client.py` drives the
    official OpenAI SDK against `ollamarun serve` (the model list, a
    completion, streaming with usage, embeddings in the SDK's default
    base64 encoding, `n > 1`, and a tools request) and `agent_client.py`
    speaks the native API over plain HTTP (submit a turn, follow the typed
    SSE event stream, resolve a parked approval, print the terminal
    summary). Both print a PASS/SKIP/FAIL line per step, exit non-zero on
    a failure, and run as the `test_examples` regression against the fake
    stack so they cannot rot; the pyflakes gate now covers `examples/` too.
  - README: a new "Example clients" section with the runnable commands, and
    the Agent API section gains "Deployment and auth" — the bind address is
    the only boundary, authentication is deliberately deferred and, when it
